@page
@model RekeyReportModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Re-key report";
}

<div class="main-content">
    <h2 style="margin:0 0 24px 0;"><sl-icon name="key" style="margin-right:8px;vertical-align:middle;"></sl-icon>Re-key report</h2>

    <div id="rekey-loading" style="text-align:center; padding:40px;">
        <sl-spinner style="font-size: 3rem;"></sl-spinner>
    </div>

    <sl-alert id="rekey-none" variant="neutral" style="display:none; margin-bottom:16px;">
        <sl-icon slot="icon" name="info-circle"></sl-icon>
        This vault has not been re-keyed.
    </sl-alert>

    <sl-alert id="rekey-error" variant="danger" style="display:none; margin-bottom:16px;">
        <sl-icon slot="icon" name="exclamation-octagon"></sl-icon>
        <span id="rekey-error-text"></span>
    </sl-alert>

    <div id="rekey-body" style="display:none;">
        <sl-alert id="rekey-result" open style="margin-bottom:16px;">
            <sl-icon slot="icon" name="info-circle"></sl-icon>
            <strong id="rekey-result-title"></strong>
            <div id="rekey-result-detail"></div>
        </sl-alert>

        <sl-card id="rekey-next" style="width:100%; margin-bottom:24px;">
            <div slot="header"><strong>What you need to do now</strong></div>
            <p>The vault now has a new key. Everything this node holds was sealed again under it, and the old key opens
                none of it. What lives outside this node was not changed:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Re-pair every blind node now.</strong> Until you do, a blind node keeps serving its old copy
                    of the vault to anyone who holds the old credentials.</li>
                <li><strong>Devices re-join as new profiles.</strong> Only your password opens this vault now.</li>
                <li><strong>Reset the other users' passwords.</strong> Their old passwords no longer sign in; each of them
                    can sign in again once you set a new password for them (Admin, Users). They are listed below.</li>
                <li><strong>Recreate agents and recovery codes.</strong> Every agent was revoked; the old agent keys,
                    recovery codes and the OS auto-unlock no longer work.</li>
                <li><strong>Old backups, snapshots and devices still open with the old key.</strong> The re-key cannot
                    reach them; delete the ones you no longer trust.</li>
                <li><strong>The old vault folder can be deleted</strong> once you have checked this vault. It still opens
                    with the old key. Deleting it on an SSD does not guarantee the bytes are erased.</li>
            </ul>
            <p id="rekey-old-vault" style="display:none;">Old vault folder: <code id="rekey-old-vault-path"></code>
                <span id="rekey-old-vault-gone" style="display:none;">(already deleted)</span></p>
        </sl-card>

        <sl-card id="rekey-warnings-card" style="width:100%; margin-bottom:24px; display:none;">
            <div slot="header"><strong>Found before the re-key</strong></div>
            <ul id="rekey-blocking"></ul>
            <ul id="rekey-warnings"></ul>
        </sl-card>

        <sl-card style="width:100%; margin-bottom:24px;">
            <div slot="header"><strong>What was done</strong></div>
            <table class="bmb-table" style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse;">
                <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>What</th><th style="text-align:right;">Rows</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody id="rekey-steps"></tbody>
            </table>
            <div id="rekey-lists"></div>
        </sl-card>
    </div>
</div>

<script src="/js/pages/rekey-report.js"></script>
